  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowered Agents of Change for Freedom of Religion or Belief 2021-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program aims to equip beneficiaries in ODA countries where serious human rights violations occur, with the necessary tools to increase the respect, protection and promotion of freedom of religion or belief for all. This includes both civil society organisations, religious and belief-based communities, decision makers and civil servants. One of the outcomes is that agents of change are aware of issues at the intersection of FoRB and gender equality and include a gender perspective in FoRB interventions. By the development of and training in, educational and legal resources, and facilitating networks between beneficiaries, the program wants to see agents of change that are actively involved in advocating for change in their respective contexts.</narrative>
  </description>
